Building Super Hoops showed me how important a clear initial plan and prompt can be. Writing a detailed prompt gave me a working 2D arcade basketball game in a single HTML file on the second try. I wanted to build a basketball game with a hoop on either side of the court with bosses that try to stop you, with powerups, and obstacles. I wanted the game to be something anyone could play and enjoy and spend time playing, instead of playing it for a minut and getting bored, which is why I added the bosses and tried to make it visually appealing. Features like the charge jump controls, moving hoops, boss fights, power ups, and sound effects all were what I asked for and ended up good. I wanted this game to be for any age, a game anyone could enjoy. The challenge I faced was getting good physics, as the ball would sometimes get stuck in the rim or in the corner. Also the rims were facing the wrong direction in my first prompt. If I were to do this again, I would spend more time expanding on the initial features and making the graphics better to create a more detailed and fully finished final game. Overall the game was created in 1 prompt but i had to give it a second prompt to finish the game and make it what i wanted and fix bugs.
